{"name":"Rolling Prairie","hex":"#a29367","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rolling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Drunk; intoxicated from alcohol, staggering.","Staggered in time and space."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of roll"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rolling"},{"term":"prairie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extensive area of relatively flat grassland with few, if any, trees, especially in North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prairie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rolling Prairie, Indiana","blocks":[{"text":"Rolling Prairie is an unincorporated community and census-designated place (CDP) in Kankakee Township, LaPorte County, Indiana, United States. As of the 2020 census, it had a population of 562."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/LaPorte_County_Indiana_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Rolling_Prairie_Highlighted_1865736.svg/330px-LaPorte_County_Indiana_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Rolling_Prairie_Highlighted_1865736.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Prairie%2C_Indiana"},{"title":"Rolling Prairie, Wisconsin","blocks":[{"text":"Rolling Prairie is an unincorporated community located between the towns of Oak Grove and Burnett in Dodge County, Wisconsin, United States."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Prairie%2C_Wisconsin"},{"title":"Rolling","blocks":[{"text":"Rolling is a type of motion that combines rotation and translation of that object with respect to a surface, such that, if ideal conditions exist, the two are in contact with each other without sliding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Rolling_animation.gif/330px-Rolling_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling"},{"title":"Prairie","blocks":[{"text":"Prairies are ecosystems considered part of the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome by ecologists, based on similar temperate climates, moderate rainfall, and a composition of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, rather than trees, as the dominant vegetation type. Temperate grassland regions include the Pampas of Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay, and the steppe of Romania, Ukraine, Russia, and Kazakhstan. Lands typically referred to as \"prairie\" tend to be in North America. The term encompasses the lower and mid-latitude of the area referred to as the Interior Plains of Canada, the United States, and Mexico. It includes all of the Great Plains as well as the wetter, hillier land to the east. From west to east, generally the drier expanse of shortgrass prairie gives way to mixed grass prairie and ultimately the richer and wetter soils of the tallgrass prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg/330px-James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prairie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Moglfm2207_rodadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Moglfm2207_rodadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoglfm2207_rodadura.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg/1280px-Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam